# Session tags

Tags are independent many-to-many memberships, not attention flags. Create two
plain live sessions and a repository with a non-live named workspace. Capture
the physical fixture directory as ROOT to normalize JSON paths to <ROOT>.

    :b jj cat sed pwd (available)
    :$ -q pwd -P (exit: 0)
    := ROOT (bound)

    :cp tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)
    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :t new-session -d -s first "cat" (success)
    :t new-session -d -s second "cat" (success)
    :$ -q smth --no-base --create-repo --create alpha (exit: 0)
    :$ -q jj workspace add -R alpha --name idle alpha.idle (exit: 0)

Both plain sessions can carry a, and first can also carry z. Repeated tagging
is idempotent. Successful mutations exit 0 without output. Flagging first must
not alter either membership; JSON lists
first's tags alphabetically and reports the flag independently.

    :$ smth --no-base --tag z first (exit: 0)
    :$ smth --no-base --tag a first (exit: 0)
    :$ smth --no-base --tag a first (exit: 0)
    :$ smth --no-base --tag a second (exit: 0)
    :$ smth --no-base --flag first (exit: 0)
    :$ smth --no-base --json --query first (exit: 0)

```stdout
[
  {
    "name": "first",
    "tmux": "first",
    "live": true,
    "deletable": false,
    "pending_deletion": false,
    "flagged": true,
    "tags": [
      "a",
      "z"
    ]
  }
]
```

Removing a twice from first must preserve z, its flag, and second's a.

    :$ smth --no-base --untag a first (exit: 0)
    :$ smth --no-base --untag a first (exit: 0)
    :$ smth --no-base --json --query first (exit: 0)

```stdout
[
  {
    "name": "first",
    "tmux": "first",
    "live": true,
    "deletable": false,
    "pending_deletion": false,
    "flagged": true,
    "tags": [
      "z"
    ]
  }
]
```

    :$ smth --no-base --json --query second (exit: 0)

```stdout
[
  {
    "name": "second",
    "tmux": "second",
    "live": true,
    "deletable": false,
    "pending_deletion": false,
    "flagged": false,
    "tags": [
      "a"
    ]
  }
]
```

A default-workspace base supplies the target when omitted. A named workspace
base does the same; an explicit operand overrides it. The tmux option queries
print 1 because each preceding command enabled that membership.

    :$ smth --base alpha --tag b (exit: 0)
    :t show-options -qv -t '=alpha:' @smth.tag.b (success)

```
1
```

    :$ -q smth --base alpha --create feature (exit: 0)
    :$ smth --base alpha.feature --tag c (exit: 0)
    :t show-options -qv -t '=alpha/feature:' @smth.tag.c (success)

```
1
```

    :$ -q smth --base alpha --create other (exit: 0)
    :$ smth --base alpha.feature --tag d other (exit: 0)
    :t show-options -qv -t '=alpha/other:' @smth.tag.d (success)

```
1
```

Closing and recreating first loses its tags and flag, while second remains
in a. Separate CLI invocations above already demonstrate persistence across
smth process exits.

    :$ smth --no-base --close first (exit: 0)
    :t new-session -d -s first "cat" (success)
    :$ smth --no-base --json --query first (exit: 0)

```stdout
[
  {
    "name": "first",
    "tmux": "first",
    "live": true,
    "deletable": false,
    "pending_deletion": false,
    "flagged": false,
    "tags": []
  }
]
```

    :$ smth --no-base --json --query second (exit: 0)

```stdout
[
  {
    "name": "second",
    "tmux": "second",
    "live": true,
    "deletable": false,
    "pending_deletion": false,
    "flagged": false,
    "tags": [
      "a"
    ]
  }
]
```

A and aa violate the lowercase single-letter constraint, missing identifies no
session, and idle has no live tmux session. These operational errors exit 1.
The non-live idle candidate has no tags field in JSON; its paths are normalized
to <ROOT> using the physical directory captured during setup.

    :$ smth --no-base --tag A first (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: tag must be one lowercase letter a-z
```

    :$ smth --no-base --tag aa first (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: tag must be one lowercase letter a-z
```

    :$ smth --no-base --tag a missing (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: session not found
```

    :$ smth --base alpha --repo 'alpha*' --tag a idle (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: session is not live
```

    :$ smth --base alpha --repo 'alpha*' --json --query idle (exit: 0)
    :| sed "s#${ROOT}#<ROOT>#g" (exit: 0)

```stdout
[
  {
    "base": "<ROOT>/alpha",
    "name": "idle",
    "path": "<ROOT>/alpha.idle",
    "tmux": "alpha/idle",
    "live": false,
    "deletable": true,
    "pending_deletion": false
  }
]
```

Tag mutations reject picker controls and other lifecycle actions during argument
parsing, producing usage diagnostics and exit 2.

    :$ smth --no-base --tag a first --query first (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: the argument '--tag <TAG> <SESSION>' cannot be used with '--query <STR>'

Usage: smth --no-base --tag <TAG> <SESSION>

For more information, try 'help'.
```

    :$ smth --no-base --tag a first --json (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: the argument '--tag <TAG> <SESSION>' cannot be used with '--json'

Usage: smth --no-base --tag <TAG> <SESSION>

For more information, try 'help'.
```

    :$ smth --no-base --tag a first --untag a first (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: the argument '--tag <TAG> <SESSION>' cannot be used with '--untag <TAG> <SESSION>'

Usage: smth --no-base --tag <TAG> <SESSION>

For more information, try 'help'.
```

